s1-1-p4 : Block
s1-1-p4 = prose (cons "A cubical context also contains interval variables and face conditions. A path is a term indexed by an interval coordinate with specified endpoints. The operations of composition, filling, Glue, and transport give computation rules for dependent paths; univalence turns an equivalence into an identification of types. Inductive and higher-inductive definitions introduce data and paths by their constructors. The clocked extension permits guarded continuing computation. The computational rules follow the CCHM cubical calculus [9], extended with clock-indexed guarded computation [44]. Their relevant operations and judgments are developed below. These rules specify how the language computes with the identities of its own constructions, including the relations used to carry reasoning across representations." nil)
